From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: Power down the controller/device during system suspend for SM8450

Like SM8550 and SM8650, the SM8450 (and SM8475, which uses the SM8450
UFS controller) UFS PHY does not retain its state across a CX power
collapse. With the default spm_lvl of UFS_PM_LVL_3 the link is left in
HIBERN8 and the device in SLEEP during system suspend. Once the SoC
reaches CX collapse, the PHY state is lost and the first transfers after
resume fail.

On a Lenovo Legion Y700 (2023, SM8475) the first s2idle that reached
AOSS/CX/DDR sleep was followed, about four seconds after resume, by UIC
PA and data-link errors, repeated host and device resets and finally
"HBA state error", failing reads and writes to the root filesystem.
Earlier s2idle cycles on the same kernel that did not reach CX collapse
resumed cleanly.

Set no_phy_retention for "qcom,sm8450-ufshc" so that hba->spm_lvl
defaults to UFS_PM_LVL_5 and the controller, device and PHY are powered
down during system suspend and fully reinitialised on resume, as already
done for SM8550/SM8650. The SM8550 LSDBS quirk does not apply to this
controller, so use a separate drvdata.

This follows upstream commit 3b2f56860b05 ("scsi: ufs: qcom: Power down
the controller/device during system suspend for SM8550/SM8650 SoCs"):
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/3b2f56860b05bf0cea86af786fd9b7faa8fe3ef3

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3004,6 +3004,10 @@
 		platform_device_msi_free_irqs_all(hba->dev);
 }
 
+static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sm8450_drvdata = {
+	.no_phy_retention = true,
+};
+
 static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata = {
 	.quirks = UFSHCD_QUIRK_BROKEN_LSDBS_CAP,
 	.no_phy_retention = true,
@@ -3015,6 +3019,7 @@
 
 static const struct of_device_id ufs_qcom_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ufshc" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8450-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8450_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8255p-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
